    "lsj_gloss": "from κάλχη, properly 'to make purple'; metaph. 'to make dark and troublous like a stormy sea, to ponder deeply'",
    "lsj_cite": "LSJ s.v. καλχαίνω (Perseus text:1999.04.0057; Middle Liddell entry n16598)",
    "root_cite": "< κάλχη 'murex, purple limpet, = πορφύρα' (LSJ s.v. κάλχη, Perseus text:1999.04.0057 entry=ka/lxh; Nicander)",
    "note": "The literal colour sense ('make purple') is the ETYMON; the classical text uses the figurative 'brood darkly' sense. Hölderlin 1804 revives the literal colour reading ('ein rothes Wort zu färben' = to dye a red/purple word); Donner 1868 takes the figurative dark reading ('Düster wogt'). This row is the source-side latent-written colour the crossing measures."
   }
  ],
  "effect": "καλχαίνω (v.20) reads latent-WRITTEN; the Hölderlin colour crossing lands REVIVAL (starred) — the paper's founding claim measured for the first time."
